    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch15-06: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.48";
    dc:description "The equation is explicit and falsifiable, but shape alone leaves too many unknown fields to test it. Existing museum geometry cannot provide a noncircular estimate of all terms.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: For eggs sampled before shell hardening, jointly measure local principal curvatures, external normal pressure, membrane tension and internal pressure, then test pointwise closure of the equation and compare residuals with richer anisotropic-shell models. Systematic nonzero residuals beyond measurement error would refute the asserted law.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Hard shells violate the extensible-membrane postulate.", "Material anisotropy and spatially varying thickness are plausible omitted terms.", "Public datasets lack co-registered membrane tension and pressure fields.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.76"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.484"^^xsd:double;
